<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Janjira State</h1><p class="st-meta">1489 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Murud</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An island fortress state on the Konkan coast ruled by Siddis of African descent, whose sea fort at Murud resisted both Shivaji and the Portuguese.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siddis">Siddis</a>, Muslims of East African (Habshi) origin, held the island fort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murud-janjira">Janjira</a> off Murud as officers of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ahmadnagar-sultanate">Ahmadnagar Sultanate</a>; tradition dates their control to 1489. They later served the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/bijapur-sultanate">Bijapur Sultanate</a> and then acted as admirals of the Mughal fleet on the west coast.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>From the island fortress the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siddis">Siddi Nawabs</a> commanded the coast south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Bombay</a> and its sea trade. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> and his son Sambhaji both failed to take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murud-janjira">Janjira</a>, despite building the rival fort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padmadurg">Padmadurg</a> nearby. The state also held <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jafrabad-state">Jafrabad</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Kathiawar</a>. Succession passed among the Siddi families rather than strictly from father to son.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murud-janjira">Janjira</a> came under British protection in the 19th century and merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombay-state">Bombay State</a> in 1948. The fort, never taken by storm, stands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raigad">Raigad</a> district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/janjira-state.jpg" alt="Janjira State" width="320" height="202"><figcaption>Image: Robert Alfers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Janjira.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1489 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Murud</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Marathi, Urdu</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>India</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Murud-Janjira, Habsan</dd></dl></aside></div>
